# What `docker build` may not send to the daemon.
#
# There was no such file. From a clean checkout that meant about 23 MB, which
# is survivable; from a working tree it meant **1.4 GB**, because
# `web/node_modules` is 715 MB and `var/` is 231 MB and neither is referenced by
# any Dockerfile here. `fly deploy` from a laptop — the documented path in
# `docs/mcp-deployment.md` — runs `--remote-only`, so that context goes over
# the network to Fly's builder. It is now 12 MB either way.
#
# The list below names the known offenders. It is not the whole defence: a
# directory nobody has thought of yet would slip past it silently, so CI also
# asserts a ceiling on the context size (`ci.yml`, the image job). This file
# keeps the number small; that check notices when something new makes it big.

# Dependency trees. Both images install their own.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
.venv/
venv/

# Build output, of every kind. `ops/Dockerfile.mcp` builds its own catalog in
# its first stage; a `var/` from somebody's laptop would be shadowed by it at
# best and stale at worst.
var/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml

# History and CI machinery. The image is built from a checkout, not a clone.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Local configuration and anything that might carry a credential. A `.env` in
# the context is a `.env` in the image if any COPY is wide enough to catch it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Editors, platforms, scratch.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Documentation and tests. `ops/Dockerfile.mcp` needs exactly one thing from
# `tests/` — the golden-set records under `tests/fixtures/records`, which are
# production content living in a test directory (see
# `data/golden-set/README.md`) — so the tree is not excluded wholesale here.
docs/
